 "note": "Neighbourhood profiles. Each neighbourhood is a union of whole census tracts, so counts are exact sums and nothing is apportioned across a boundary. Medians are ranges because medians cannot be averaged; percentages are weighted by tract population or housing units. Asset counts are what falls inside the boundary, which is not the same as what is within walking distance of it.",
